+# Executive referee — `optimal-play-lemma-d-restricted-n7-20261123`
+
+Date: 2026-11-23 ~16:45Z. Office: executive, billy-dev. Independent executive
+delivery, NOT a parliamentary sitting and NOT Clerk intake. Additive record.
+
+## Source and scope
+
+- Refereed RESULT: #301 comment 2026-11-23T16:19:40Z, id
+  `sha256:RR6qQ7bcxdKDqykpS0k0avCAvhK60tr26ba-OKPMpSM`, front
+  `optimal-play-lemma-d-restricted-n7-20261123` (agent `TKK9KmUgDzyAzA4VvjY8gE-sans`,
+  the follow-up dispatched at 15:29Z).
+- My only external writes: the #301 referee comment 2026-11-23T16:44:55Z, id
+  `sha256:OJx2pq3PMbSivCvuOSySgUysv_JT3GT6AyoZZ8m1w6o`, and this Act 31 record.
+- No theorem completion for S(n)/SORT-BOUND-U; no repo/Lean/test/CI/ledger/
+  canonical-main/bill/ballot/case change. S(n) and SORT-BOUND-U remain OPEN.
+
+## Question
+
+R_7 = states reachable from the 7-antichain A_7 by k-safe comparisons at
+budget k=S(7)=13 (a comparison at depth d admitted only if both outcome
+children have d+1+F <= 13). Is F a function of (e,M1) on R_7, where e is the
+number of linear extensions and M1 is the sorted multiset of e-values of all
+one-step children over both orientations of every incomparable pair?
+
+## Verdict: ACCEPT the finite n=7 structural fact
+
+I independently reproduced every numerical deliverable with a from-scratch
+implementation of a different design; I did not read or reuse the reporter's
+code or scratch artifacts.
+
+### My independent verifier
+
+`/tmp/opencode/referee_r7_indep.cpp`, compiled with clang 19.1.7 at -O2 (a guix
+toolchain). Design:
+
+- Poset = 7x7 transitive-closure bitmask; 42-bit key encodes both orientations
+  of each of the 21 unordered pairs.
+- e(P) by subset DP over 2^7 subsets: f[0]=1,
+  f[m] = sum over i maximal in P|m of f[m\{i}], e(P)=f[full].
+- Child counts cnt[x][y]=e(P+x<y) in closed form over ideals:
+  sum over ideals m with x in m, y not in m, pred(y) subset of m of
+  f[m] * f[(V\m)\{y}] (y minimal in the complement).
+- F by memoized minimax: F=0 if e=1, else
+  1 + min over incomparable pairs of max(F(c1),F(c2)).
+- k-safe forward BFS from A_7: admit a child at depth d+1 only when
+  (d+1)+F(child) <= 13; record minimal discovery depth.
+- M1 = sorted multiset of 2*(number of incomparable pairs) child-e values.
+
+### Reproduced exactly
+
+- F(A_7)=13=S(7); e(A_7)=5040.
+- |R_7| = 3,044,007 with the identical depth histogram
+  d0..d13 = 1, 42, 840, 9240, 64470, 328020, 968534, 1165080, 466620,
+  39900, 1260, 0, 0, 0 (sums to 3,044,007; d1=42=C(7,2)*2).
+- 392 distinct (e,M1) keys over R_7; 0 keys with more than one F value.
+- The conflict signature e=32,
+  M1=(4,4,14,14,16,16,16,16,16,16,18,18,28,28), occurs in R_7 with F=5
+  only; no F=6 member.
+- Globally, over all 6,129,859 labeled n=7 posets (my memo size, matching
+  A001035(7)): exactly ONE conflicting (e,M1) key, the same e=32 signature
+  with F in {5,6}; restricted to that key, F5=5040, F6=2520, total 7560.
+
+### Audit of my own process
+
+Three intermediate disagreements with the reported numbers were traced to bugs
+in MY verifier: (1) a one-orientation poset key colliding for i<j vs j<i;
+(2) an up-set instead of down-set ideal test; (3) a 16-bit overflow in a count
+product. After fixing those, my output matched on every listed deliverable.
+Recorded because a first-pass mismatch is evidence to audit, not a result to
+hide.
+
+## Scope and caution
+
+- Finite n=7 fact about k-safe-reachable states at k=S(7)=13. It does not
+  extend Lemma D to all n, does not compute or bound S(n), and has no
+  SORT-BOUND-U/class consequence.
+- I do NOT adopt the informal "e=32 requires depth >= 8" motivation as a proof.
+  The implicit "each comparison at most halves e" bound is false in general:
+  an unbalanced comparison can reduce e by less than a factor of 2 (e.g. from
+  e=3 on three elements to a child of e=1). The reachability conclusion rests
+  on the exhaustive BFS, which I independently reproduced.
+
